A||||10||88formula||AutoXray EZ link scanner?||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||08-05-2001||12:40 AM||||Do any of you have this scanner? Is it any good or is it a POS. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero_Freak||08-05-2001||09:54 AM||||I have the one that does OBD I and II.  It works great and has helped be track down quite a few problems.  I've probably saved what I paid for it in gas since I've corrected quite a few semi-defective parts.  I got mine off e-bay for about 250+shipping.  It was practically new.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg"> <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||08-05-2001||11:02 AM||||I've got one too, when I bought mine it was cheaper to buy just the OBD-I kit and the OBD-II cable separately rather than the integrated kit.<P>It's an expensive toy if you just want it to look for error codes, but if you want to look real time at what most of the sensors are reporting to the ECM it's great.  Stuff like open/closed loop mode, engine RPM, EGR duty cycle, injector pulse duration, coolant and intake manifold temps, and most of the sensor output voltages can be tracked in real time. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||08-05-2001||11:10 AM||||I have the Pro Pack with all the cables and I have really got a lot of use out of it so far. Really comes in handy when you are tuning chips because it shows a lot of information.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||08-05-2001||12:10 PM||||I've had their OBD I self contained scanner fro a couple years now. wouldn't have been able to do half the engine stuff I've done w/o it. It is the only way you can reliably do anything with a DIS motor. The stand alone units do have some logging built in. <P>The PC based scanners are nice if you have a laptop or a garage for a "desktop" to be setup. They are even better if you can select multiple things to view at once. To make one of these really usefull, you're laptop has to have a good battery. You want to be able to drive the car while the PC logs the signals. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||08-05-2001||01:45 PM||||OK thanks guys. I need one for my 3.4 formula. The stock 2.8 programing isn't working with my 3.4 engine very well. I can't get it to run with the new 2.8 injectors and it runs rather crappy with the used 3.4 injectors. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||08-05-2001||04:51 PM||||You definatly need a scanner. You need to check all the other sensors before you start fooling with chips. One of them may be bad or marginal. <P>You also need to check all the wiring and gounds one more time at least. A bad/missing ground strap will do all sorts of nasty things to engine performance.||||reg||1
